# Build context exclusions (M8 Task 1).
#
# Two jobs. The obvious one is image size. The one that matters more is that
# `COPY . .` puts everything the daemon received into a layer, and a layer is
# readable by anyone who can pull the image -- deleting a file in a later
# instruction does not remove it from the earlier one. Secrets and measurement
# data must never enter the context in the first place.
#
# The runtime stages now COPY only `src/`, so this is defence in depth rather
# than the only control. Both are kept: a future COPY that widens its scope
# should not be able to leak.

# --- Secrets: the reason this file is not optional ---
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# --- Version control ---
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Python build and cache artefacts ---
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Local environments ---
.venv
venv
env

# --- Measurement output. Never runtime input. ---
# reports/ holds the observability JSONL and every generated answer, including the
# full text of what the LLM produced during evaluation. reports/ is mounted as a
# volume in compose, so excluding it from the context does not remove it at run
# time -- it removes it from the image.
reports/
tests/eval/results/

# --- Tests, tooling and data. Nothing under src/ imports any of it. ---
tests/
scripts/
notebooks/
docs/
database/
configs/
data/
*.ipynb

# --- Model caches. The API image bakes the model in the builder stage instead. ---
.cache
huggingface
sentence_transformers
models

# --- Editor and OS noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Docs and dead files ---
README_old.md
*.md
!README.md
